{
  "requirement": "A paragraph has no declared name. Each prose paragraph has an anonymous\n`paragraph` node under its nearest\nenclosing outline container. This includes paragraphs before the first heading\nand inside list items, quotations, and directive bodies. Their selectors follow\n{cite}`requirements.references.outline_selectors`. Heading text and literal\ncode-block contents create no paragraph nodes. Syntax that has no outline node\nis transparent when finding the enclosing container.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The marked tests cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.sources.markdown.paragraphs`. I read the tests and the Markdown implementation. I used the implementation only to see why the first node in the preamble test is a section. It is the anonymous preamble section, which `requirements.sdk.sources.markdown.sections` allows.\n\n**Anonymous `paragraph` nodes under the nearest container**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/markdown_tests.rs#fn[paragraphs_and_nested_directives_have_independent_source_ranges]` asserts exact kind, parent and source range for each node in a section containing a paragraph, a `note` directive with a paragraph, and a nested `tip` directive with its own paragraph.\n- It checks that each paragraph's parent is its enclosing section or directive block.\n- It also checks that each paragraph segment is `paragraph@` plus 12 hash characters, so the name is anonymous.\n\n**Paragraphs before the first heading, in list items, in quotations, and in directive bodies**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/markdown_tests.rs#fn[paragraphs_in_transparent_lists_and_quotes_are_selectable]` has a paragraph before any heading, a list-item paragraph, a block-quote paragraph, and a paragraph after a setext heading.\n- It asserts exactly four paragraph nodes at the expected start lines.\n- The first three have the preamble container as parent, so the list and quote syntax is transparent.\n- The last has `section[Title]` as parent.\n- Directive bodies are covered by the first test, including the nested one.\n\n**Selectors follow `requirements.references.outline_selectors`**\n- The first test calls `outline.resolve(&node.selector)` for every node and checks that it returns that node's index. It also checks `node_lines` against the byte range.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/markdown_tests.rs#fn[anonymous_identities_survive_reflow_and_sibling_edits_and_number_duplicates]` checks that paragraph selectors are stable under reflow and sibling edits.\n- It also checks that the structural hash changes when content changes.\n- It checks that duplicate paragraphs get numbered suffixes.\n\n**Heading text creates no paragraph**\n- The ATX heading in the first test and the setext heading in the second yield no paragraph nodes. The exact kind list and the exact paragraph count prove this.\n\n**Literal code-block contents create no paragraph**\n- In the first test, the fenced block containing `hi` has no paragraph child, and the kind list is exact.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/markdown_tests.rs#fn[literal_code_inline_code_and_html_shield_directive_looking_text]` (marked for `fenced_blocks.contents`, not for this requirement) also asserts no paragraph nodes from code content.\n\nI found no behaviour that violates the requirement and would pass these tests. Untested combinations, such as lists inside directives, are not distinguished by the requirement. The citation of `requirements.references.outline_selectors` needs no extra coverage.",
